From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:30:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: schedule a station's txqs on the hw it belongs to

mt76_tx_check_non_aql() re-armed a station's txqs on dev->hw. With DBDC
chips such as MT7986 the second band is a separate ieee80211_hw, so a
station on it was put on band 0's active txq list, under band 0's
active_txq_lock, while band 1's mac80211 kept using the same txq with
its own. mt76_txq_schedule_list() then switched phy to the station's
and kept calling ieee80211_next_txq() on the other hw for the rest of
the pass.

Re-arm on the station's own hw, and keep iterating the hw the
scheduling round was started on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tx.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tx.c b/tx.c
index 0060cfa8..05d73ac4 100644
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -253,7 +253,8 @@ mt76_tx_check_non_aql(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_wcid *wcid,
 		if (!sta->txq[i])
 			continue;
 
-		ieee80211_schedule_txq(dev->hw, sta->txq[i]);
+		ieee80211_schedule_txq(mt76_phy_hw(dev, wcid->phy_idx),
+				       sta->txq[i]);
 	}
 }
 
@@ -572,6 +573,7 @@ out:
 static int
 mt76_txq_schedule_list(struct mt76_phy *phy, enum mt76_txq_id qid)
 {
+	struct ieee80211_hw *hw = phy->hw;
 	struct mt76_dev *dev = phy->dev;
 	struct ieee80211_txq *txq;
 	struct mt76_txq *mtxq;
@@ -582,7 +584,8 @@ mt76_txq_schedule_list(struct mt76_phy *phy, enum mt76_txq_id qid)
 	while (1) {
 		int n_frames = 0;
 
-		txq = ieee80211_next_txq(phy->hw, qid);
+		/* keep iterating the hw that schedule_start() was called on */
+		txq = ieee80211_next_txq(hw, qid);
 		if (!txq)
 			break;
 
